ADDENDA <Act No. 20909, Apr. 8, 2025>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Article 30 (1) and (3) shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to report on changed contents of game products)
The amended provisions of Article 21 (5) and (6) shall begin to apply to the cases where reports are filed on the changed contents of game products after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to re-designation of independent rating classification business entities)
The amended provisions of Article 21-6 (2) shall also apply to cases where a person who is designated as an independent rating classification business entity under Article 21-2 before this Act enters into force is re-designated.
Article 4 (Applicability to matters to be observed by rating classification agencies)
The amended provisions of Article 24-3 shall also apply to the rating classification agencies entrusted with the rating classification affairs under Article 24-2 before this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Applicability to reports on business closure of game producing business)
The amended provisions of Article 30 (1) shall begin to apply where a person who has been granted a license or completed registration or filed a report under Article 25 or 26 discontinues his or her business after that amended provisions enter into force.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning entrustment of rating classification affairs)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 24-2 (1), the previous provisions shall apply to the determination of rating classification of game products, notification of game products subject to rating reclassification, and measures, etc. applied before this Act enters into force.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 24-2 (1), the previous provisions shall apply to the acceptance of reports, etc. on the changed contents of game products which are filed before this Act enters into force.
